# QA Suspended (Owner Mandate — wins over mandatory QA rules)

**Status: SUSPENDED** (owner mandate, 2026-08-30).

While `docs/qa/QA_SUSPENDED.flag` exists:

## Forbidden

- Run **any** automated QA suite (planning gate, SSOT gates, class gates, live QA, regression, swap, T3 mimic, scene acceptance, full QA, background class tests)
- Invoke Godot test harnesses for QA purposes (`GdUnitCmdTool`, `*QaGate.tscn`, `run_*_qa*.ps1`, `run_regression_tests.ps1`)
- Report QA PASS/FAIL in changelog for gameplay edits
- Suggest "let me run QA" or use QA output to justify architecture compliance

## Required instead

- Implement planning SSOT architecture fixes only
- Architecture compliance verdict: **yes** or **no** against the four criteria in `docs/qa/QA_SUSPENSION.md` — not QA pass/fail

## Sentinel + scripts

`scripts/qa/qa_suspend_guard.ps1` is dot-sourced from QA entry helpers. If the flag exists, scripts exit `99` with `[QA SUSPENDED]`.

## Re-enable (owner only)

Owner must **both**:

1. Delete `docs/qa/QA_SUSPENDED.flag`
2. Say explicitly in chat: **"QA is re-enabled"** or **"planning SSOT is 100% compliant — run QA"**

Until then, QA stays off permanently.

## Wins over

- `.cursor/rules/qa-after-gameplay-changes.mdc` (mandatory QA after gameplay edits)
- `.cursor/rules/class-qa-all-classes-mandatory.mdc` (QA run portions)
- `.cursor/rules/class-qa-knight-bar.mdc` (QA run portions)
- `AGENTS.md` test execution hierarchy (QA runs)
